{
  "description": "WorkspaceJail.check(path) and pathShapes(path) over the workspace described in `layout` (paths relative to the workspace root; symlink targets relative to the link; `outside` files live beside the root in its parent). `<root>` in an input stands for the absolute, canonical workspace root and `<base>` for its parent — in an output, also for the parent with its leading `/` removed, which is what clamping an absolute path that is not under the root leaves behind. `output.check` is {ok: true, relative, canonical, rewrites} — `relative` is the verdict's clamped workspace-relative form and `canonical` is the verified path relative to the root (they differ when a symlink was resolved), both with `/` separators — or {ok: false, rejection, message}. `output.shapes` is pathShapes(), the pre-chroot syntactic rule the exec guard refuses on. The 4096-character name is `unverifiable` because the filesystem answers ENAMETOOLONG.",
  "layout": {
    "files": [
      "here.txt",
      "real/file.txt",
      "a/b.txt"
    ],
    "directories": [
      "real",
      "a",
      "nested/dir"
    ],
    "symlinks": {
      "alias": "real",
      "alias.txt": "../outside/secret.txt",
      "escape": "../outside",
      "up": "..",
      "vault": "../vault.json",
      "link": "../gone"
    },
    "outside": [
      "outside/secret.txt"
    ]
  },
